<title>INDIA: India approves IBM 720-mln-rupee unit.</title>
<headline>India approves IBM 720-mln-rupee unit.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Indian Industry Ministry said on Wednesday it approved a 720-million-rupee investment by a unit of International Business Machines Corp (IBM) in an 80-percent owned computer software subsidiary.  </p>
<p>The investment was among 58 proposals worth a total of 6.6 billion rupees which were approved by the Foreign Investment Promotion Board, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>IBM World Trade Corp will set up the computer software unit in the southern city of Bangalore, it said.</p>
<p>-- New Delhi newsroom +91-11 301 2024</p>
